WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Every constant on a control chart is derived, not decreed.

2
00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:08.094
Take a subgroup of five parts off the process.

3
00:00:08.183 --> 00:00:13.075
Each part lands somewhere. Sigma itself you cannot measure.

4
00:00:13.166 --> 00:00:17.266
The range you can: largest value minus smallest.

5
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.013
Repeat forever, and the mean range settles at a

6
00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:24.858
fixed multiple of sigma. That multiple is d two.

7
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.911
spc-lab computes d two by simulating four hundred

8
00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:32.890
thousand subgroups, rather than reading a table.

9
00:00:33.583 --> 00:00:35.790
So R bar over d two estimates

10
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.051
sigma, from ranges you actually measured.

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.747
Feed that into three sigma limits, then divide by

12
00:00:42.847 --> 00:00:46.370
root n, because you are charting subgroup means.

13
00:00:46.466 --> 00:00:50.377
Gather the constants: A two equals three, over

14
00:00:50.477 --> 00:00:53.254
d two times the square root of n.

15
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.932
At n of five that is zero point

16
00:00:56.032 --> 00:01:00.258
five seven seven, matching the AIAG table exactly.

